      "summary_source": "New research suggests a “massive and untapped” opportunity for conservation within commercial concessions in Southeast Asia, reports Mongabay’s Carolyn Cowan. Using satellite data, researchers identified roughly 42 million hectares (104 million acres) of intact forest still standing inside logging, timber, rubber and oil palm concessions across Cambodia, Indonesia, Malaysia and Myanmar. The study suggests that […]",
      "summary_zh": "新研究表明，东南亚商业特许经营区内仍保存有约 4200 万公顷的完整森林，清除这些森林可能在未来 30 年内释放 12 亿吨二氧化碳。研究指出，按当前每吨 5 至 12 美元的碳价，仅依靠碳市场激励特许经营商保护森林在经济上并不可行，需要辅以绿色金融和生态系统服务付费等更广泛的融资组合。",
      "theme_zh": "碳市场与森林保护",
